                            <span style="display: inline-block; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: #f59e0b; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #f59e0b;"></span>
                            <strong style="color: #f59e0b; font-family: var(--font-mono);">#f59e0b / Amber</strong>
                          </div>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <span style="background: rgba(245,158,11,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.35); color: #fbbf24; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72rem; font-family: var(--font-mono);">WARNING / DEGRADED</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #cbd5e1; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem;">
                          Memory RSS &ge; 40.0 MiB (&lt; 10 MiB safe)<br>
                          P99 Latency &ge; 20.0 ms<br>
                          Circuit Breaker: HALF-OPEN<br>
                          WAL Delta &gt; 80% (6,550/8,192)
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #fbbf24; font-weight: 600;">
                          &bull; DEGRADED: High Memory Pressure<br>
                          &bull; DEGRADED: P99 Tail Latency Spiking<br>
                          &bull; WARNING: Circuit Breaker HALF-OPEN
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.45;">
                          <strong style="color: #f1f5f9;">Impending capacity constraint.</strong> Buffer nearing compaction threshold, or AST translation queue experiencing contention. SRE should check worker thread concurrency or verify WAL pruning.
                        </td>
                      </tr>

                      <!-- 3. Crimson Red -->
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);">
                        <td style="padding: 12px; white-space: nowrap;">
                          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
                            <span style="display: inline-block; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: #ef4444; box-shadow: 0 0 10px #ef4444;"></span>
                            <strong style="color: #ef4444; font-family: var(--font-mono);">#ef4444 / Crimson</strong>
                          </div>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <span style="background: rgba(239,68,68,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(239,68,68,0.4); color: #f87171; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72rem; font-family: var(--font-mono);">CRITICAL / ALARM</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #cbd5e1; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem;">
                          WAN Packets &gt; 0 (Egress leak)<br>
                          Circuit Breaker: OPEN<br>
                          Memory RSS &ge; 46.0 MiB (Near OOM)<br>
                          SSE Disconnected (Socket Drop)
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #f87171; font-weight: 600;">
                          &bull; SECURITY ALARM: WAN Egress Detected!<br>
                          &bull; CRITICAL: Circuit Breaker OPEN<br>
                          &bull; CRITICAL: Memory OOM Near Cap<br>
                          &bull; ALARM: Disconnected (Reconnecting)
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.45;">
                          <strong style="color: #ef4444;">Critical service or security incident.</strong> If WAN &gt; 0, an unauthorized outbound packet was detected and blocked by kernel eBPF. If Breaker is OPEN, incoming AST translations are shed to prevent OOM panic. Immediate SRE investigation required.
                        </td>
                      </tr>

                      <!-- 4. Cyan / Neon Blue -->
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);">
                        <td style="padding: 12px; white-space: nowrap;">
                          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
                            <span style="display: inline-block; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: #00e5ff; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #00e5ff;"></span>
                            <strong style="color: #00e5ff; font-family: var(--font-mono);">#00e5ff / #38bdf8</strong>
                          </div>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <span style="background: rgba(0,229,255,0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(0,229,255,0.3); color: #38bdf8; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72rem; font-family: var(--font-mono);">ATTESTATION</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #cbd5e1; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem;">
                          Storage Disk = 0.00 GB<br>
                          Flux Invariant &delta; &equiv; 0.0000<br>
                          AST Transpiler Active
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #38bdf8; font-weight: 600;">
                          &bull; Storage Footprint: 0.00 GB Disk<br>
                          &bull; Pure RAM (Zero Disk Writes)<br>
                          &bull; Invariant SAT &bull; Thm 2 &radic;
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.45;">
                          <strong style="color: #f1f5f9;">Cryptographic proof of non-persistence.</strong> Certifies that zero bytes of persistent EBS/SAN disk are allocated, and Kirchhoff telemetric flux conservation guarantees zero hidden drops across subnets.
                        </td>
                      </tr>

                      <!-- 5. Purple / Violet -->
                      <tr>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; white-space: nowrap;">
                          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
                            <span style="display: inline-block; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: #c084fc; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #c084fc;"></span>
                            <strong style="color: #c084fc; font-family: var(--font-mono);">#c084fc / Purple</strong>
                          </div>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <span style="background: rgba(168,85,247,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(168,85,247,0.35); color: #c084fc; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72rem; font-family: var(--font-mono);">CONTROL PLANE</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #cbd5e1; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem;">
                          Tier 1 In-VPC Autonomous Daemon<br>
                          Raft Cluster Quorum State<br>
                          P90 Latency Tail Range
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #c084fc; font-weight: 600;">
                          &bull; Tier 1 &bull; In-VPC Autonomous Daemon<br>
                          &bull; LEADER (Term 4)<br>
                          &bull; P90 90th Percentile
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.45;">
                          <strong style="color: #f1f5f9;">Quorum &amp; Topology Identity.</strong> Identifies distributed consensus cluster leadership, distributed term numbers, and 90th percentile response curves across all monitored VPC boundaries.
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>

                <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 0.76rem; color: #94a3b8; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
                  <span style="color: #38bdf8;">ℹ️</span>
                  <span><strong>On-Call SRE Note:</strong> When investigating any alert or telemetry anomaly on <code style="color: #38bdf8;">http://localhost:8000/dashboard</code>, always verify that the top Control Plane indicator displays <strong>#39ff14 Neon Green (Verified Stable)</strong> before escalating VPC workload incidents.</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- =========================================================================
                   SRE Self-Troubleshooting Click Navigator Runbook & Decision Tree
                   ========================================================================= -->
              <div id="admin-sre-navigator" style="background: rgba(11, 17, 32, 0.9); border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.4); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; box-shadow: 0 12px 35px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);">
                <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-bottom: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px;">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                    <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">🛠️</span>
                    <div>
                      <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: #fff; margin: 0;">
                        <span class="dcouplr-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="dcouplr-text">dcouplr</span><span class="dcouplr-bracket">/&gt;</span> SRE Self-Troubleshooting Click Navigator Runbook
                      </h3>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.76rem; color: #94a3b8; font-family: var(--font-mono); margin-top: 3px;">
                        Interactive 6-Step Autonomous Diagnostic Checklist &amp; 1-Click Remediation Playbook
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
                    <span style="background: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.4); color: #00e5ff; font-weight: 700; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7rem; font-family: var(--font-mono);">ZERO-TICKET SLA</span>
                    <a href="http://localhost:8000/dashboard" target="_blank" style="color: #38bdf8; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.76rem; font-weight: 600;">
                      Open Live Dashboard ↗
                    </a>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <p style="font-size: 0.84rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                  When an engineer or operator notices an alert or elevated indicator on the <strong style="color: #00e5ff;">Observer Performance Indicators</strong> panel, they do <em>not</em> need to file a support ticket immediately. The <strong style="color: #fff;">SRE Self-Troubleshooting Click Navigator</strong> provides a guided 6-step diagnostic checklist and 1-click execution actions that remediate 95%+ of transient anomalies directly in-memory ($0.00 cloud egress).
                </p>

                <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                  <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.8rem; text-align: left;">
                    <thead>
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); color: #94a3b8;">
                        <th style="padding: 10px 12px; width: 80px;">Step #</th>
                        <th style="padding: 10px 12px; width: 170px;">Subsystem &amp; Symptom</th>
                        <th style="padding: 10px 12px; width: 180px;">1-Click UI Button</th>
                        <th style="padding: 10px 12px; width: 220px;">API Endpoint &amp; Action</th>
                        <th style="padding: 10px 12px;">Expected Resolution &amp; Verification</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                      <!-- Step 1 -->
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);">
                        <td style="padding: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8;">STEP 01</td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <strong style="color: #f1f5f9;">Engine Latency &amp; Pulse</strong><br>
                          <span style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #94a3b8;">P99 latency &gt; 20ms or thread contention</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <span style="background: rgba(6,182,212,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.35); color: #38bdf8; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72rem;">🔍 Run Diagnostic Sweep</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #cbd5e1;">
                          <code>POST /v1/telemetry/actions/diagnostics-triage</code>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.45;">
                          Sweeps all 8 subsystems in &lt; 50ms. Flags whether AST transpiler or background garbage collection is stalling and verifies sub-5ms SLA compliance.
                        </td>
                      </tr>

                      <!-- Step 2 -->
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);">
                        <td style="padding: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8;">STEP 02</td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <strong style="color: #f1f5f9;">Circuit Breaker Tripped</strong><br>
                          <span style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #ef4444;">State: OPEN / HALF-OPEN (Traffic Shed)</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <span style="background: rgba(245,158,11,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.35); color: #fbbf24; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72rem;">⚡ 1-Click Reset Breaker</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #cbd5e1;">
                          <code>POST /v1/telemetry/actions/circuit-breaker-reset</code>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.45;">
                          Force-resets state machine to <strong style="color: #34d399;">CLOSED</strong>, zeroes consecutive failure counters, and re-arms sub-20ms trip protection. Traffic flow resumes immediately.
                        </td>
                      </tr>

                      <!-- Step 3 -->
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);">
                        <td style="padding: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8;">STEP 03</td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <strong style="color: #f1f5f9;">Memory Pressure / WAL Lag</strong><br>
                          <span style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #fbbf24;">RSS &gt; 40 MiB or &Delta;I &gt; 4,000</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px;">
                          <span style="background: rgba(16,185,129,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(16,185,129,0.35); color: #34d399; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72rem;">🧹 1-Click Flush WAL</span>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #cbd5e1;">
                          <code>POST /v1/telemetry/actions/wal-compaction</code>
                        </td>
                        <td style="padding: 12px; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.45;">
                          Truncates uncommitted WAL transaction entries, trims circular ring buffer, drops &Delta;I to 0, and restores memory headroom (&gt; 15 MiB safe margin) with zero persistent disk I/O.
                        </td>
                      </tr>

                      <!-- Step 4 -->
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);">
