              <!-- 3. Proprietary Invariant Query Calculus (Q_DCL) & Zero-Egress In-VPC Monitoring Section -->
              <div id="admin-invariant-calculus" style="margin-bottom: 3rem; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.95), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.9)); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.35); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.75rem; box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem;">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem;">
                    <span style="font-size: 1.4rem;">📐</span>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">
                      3. Proprietary Agnostic Invariant Query Calculus (&Qopf;<sub>DCL</sub>) &amp; In-VPC Autonomous Telemetry
                    </h3>
                  </div>
                  <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;">
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.15); color: #39ff14; border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.3); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">100% DETERMINISTIC</span>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.15); color: #38bdf8; border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">$0.00 EGRESS GUARANTEED</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                  Traditional observability forces organizations into vendor DSL lock-in (Datadog DSL, PromQL, NRQL, KQL) and high Cloud NAT Gateway egress taxes ($0.09/GB). 
                  <span class="dcouplr-brand-tag"><span class="tag-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="tag-name">dcouplr</span><span class="tag-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> establishes a proprietary, closed-form <em>Canonical Invariant Query Calculus (&Qopf;<sub>DCL</sub>)</em> that evaluates telemetry as topological graph invariants over closed subnets with zero cloud egress, collision-free hashing, 100% determinism (zero hallucination), and sub-16MB RAM overhead.
                </p>

                <!-- Core Pillars Grid -->
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
                  <!-- Pillar 1 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="color: #39ff14; font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-mono);">01.</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; color: #f8fafc; margin: 0;">Topological Graph Calculus (G_VPC)</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      Models the entire VPC as a directed multi-graph <code>G_VPC = (V, E, &tau;)</code> across all CIDRs, subnets, ENIs, VMs, route tables, and security groups. Invariant predicates <code>&Iota;(G_VPC, &tau;) &equiv; True</code> guarantee global operational equilibrium.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #38bdf8;">
                      &Iota;(G_VPC, &tau;) &equiv; &bigwedge; P_node(v, &tau;) &and; &bigwedge; F_flow(e, &tau;)
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Pillar 2 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="color: #39ff14; font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-mono);">02.</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; color: #f8fafc; margin: 0;">Kirchhoff Flow Conservation (Zero Blind Spots)</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      Solves cloud provider blind spots (silent hypervisor ENI drops, NAT gateway port exhaustion, security group state table drops) by mathematically enforcing flux equality: <code>&Phi;_in = &Phi;_out + &Delta;Buffer + Drops</code>.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #34d399;">
                      &delta; = &Phi;_in - (&Phi;_out + &Delta;B + D) &equiv; 0 (Proven Zero Loss)
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Pillar 3 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="color: #39ff14; font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-mono);">03.</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; color: #f8fafc; margin: 0;">128-Bit Collision-Free Hashing</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      Hierarchical URN addressing <code>dcl://vpc/subnet/node/metric</code> indexed via 128-bit HighwayHash. Collision probability across 10<sup>9</sup> metrics bounded to <code>p &lt; 1.47 &times; 10<sup>-21</sup></code> (statistically zero).
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #a78bfa;">
                      Pr(Collision) &asymp; N&sup2; / (2 &times; 2&sup1;&sup2;&sup8;) &lt; 10&macr;&sup1;&sup9;
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Pillar 4 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="color: #39ff14; font-weight: 800; font-family: var(--font-mono);">04.</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; color: #f8fafc; margin: 0;">Streaming Welford Engine (&lt; 16MB RAM)</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      Eliminates heavy TSDB index bloat and GC pauses. One-pass recurrence computes mean &mu;<sub>k</sub> and sample variance &sigma;<sub>k</sub>&sup2; in O(1) space (24 bytes per metric) and &lt; 12 CPU cycles per sample.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #fbbf24;">
                      Memory: &lt; 16 MiB RAM | Host Overhead: &lt; 0.1% CPU
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Architectural Comparison Table -->
                <div style="overflow-x: auto; background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                  <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.82rem; color: #cbd5e1; text-align: left;">
                    <thead>
                      <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);">
