              <!-- =========================================================================
                   4. Full-Stack Suite: Embedded Raft Consensus, Quorum Decision Governance & Dynamic Membership
                   ========================================================================= -->
              <div id="admin-raft-consensus-quorum" style="margin-bottom: 3rem; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.95), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.92)); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.4); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.75rem; box-shadow: 0 10px 35px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);">
                <!-- Header Banner -->
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem;">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem;">
                    <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">🏛️</span>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">
                      4. <span class="dcouplr-wordmark"><span class="dcouplr-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="dcouplr-text">dcouplr</span><span class="dcouplr-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> Full-Stack Suite: Embedded Raft Consensus, Quorum Decision Governance &amp; Dynamic Membership
                    </h3>
                  </div>
                  <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.4); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">SPEC-EDITION2-RAFT-CONSENSUS-001</span>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.15); color: #39ff14; border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.3); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">3-NODE QUORUM ACTIVE</span>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.15); color: #38bdf8; border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">ZERO-EGRESS IN-MEMORY MESH</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                  In <span class="dcouplr-brand-tag"><span class="tag-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="tag-name">dcouplr</span><span class="tag-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> <strong>Full-Stack Suite</strong>, the migration control plane is completely decentralized into an in-memory, zero-egress distributed state machine powered by embedded <strong>HashiCorp Raft consensus</strong>. The cluster guarantees strict linearizability, atomic log compaction, and deterministic multi-cloud routing without relying on external cloud databases (e.g. AWS DynamoDB, GCP Cloud Spanner, or etcd).
                </p>

                <!-- Core Governance Answer Banner -->
                <div style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
                    <span style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #c084fc;">❓</span>
                    <h4 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">
                      Authoritative Question: &ldquo;Who Decides Who Becomes Part of the Quorum in the 3-Node Quorum Active Cluster?&rdquo;
                    </h4>
                  </div>
                  <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                    Quorum decision governance in the <span class="dcouplr-wordmark"><span class="dcouplr-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="dcouplr-text">dcouplr</span><span class="dcouplr-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> Full-Stack Suite is not governed by a single point of failure or an external service. Instead, it is enforced through a <strong>4-Layer Defense-in-Depth Model</strong>: 
                    Human SREs seed initial failure domains via IaC &rarr; Active Nodes autonomously elect Leaders &rarr; The Elected Leader controls Learner-to-Voter transitions &rarr; SPIFFE mTLS cryptographically rejects unauthorized nodes at the TCP boundary.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <!-- 4-Layer Hierarchy Grid -->
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                  <!-- Layer 1 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.15); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">LAYER 1: SRE / IaC SEED</span>
                      <span style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: #64748b;">Genesis Phase</span>
                    </div>
                    <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Static Bootstrapping Declarations</h4>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <strong>Who Decides:</strong> The Cloud Platform / SRE Engineer.<br/>
                      <strong>How:</strong> The initial 3 voting nodes are declared in <code>peers.json</code>, Terraform, or Helm charts. <span class="dcouplr-wordmark"><span class="dcouplr-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="dcouplr-text">dcouplr</span><span class="dcouplr-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> Full-Stack Suite mandates distributing voters across 3 isolated failure domains (e.g. AWS <code>us-east-1</code>, AWS <code>us-west-2</code>, GCP <code>us-central1</code>). <code>raft.BootstrapCluster()</code> writes the genesis log entry at index 1.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #38bdf8;">
                      peers: [agent-01 (AZ1), agent-02 (AZ2), agent-03 (GCP)]
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Layer 2 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: #39ff14; background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.15); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">LAYER 2: PROTOCOL FSM</span>
                      <span style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: #64748b;">Autonomous</span>
                    </div>
                    <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Autonomous Runtime Elections</h4>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <strong>Who Decides:</strong> The Active Member Nodes.<br/>
                      <strong>How:</strong> No human or central coordinator is involved. Leader sends heartbeats every 50ms. If heartbeat drops for &gt;200ms, a follower transitions to Candidate and requests votes. With 2 of 3 votes (&lfloor;3/2&rfloor; + 1 = 2), it self-elects as the new LEADER in &lt;100ms.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #39ff14;">
                      Heartbeat: 50ms &bull; Timeout: 200ms &bull; 2/3 Majority
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Layer 3 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: #c084fc; background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.15); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">LAYER 3: LEADER LOG COMMIT</span>
                      <span style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: #64748b;">Dynamic</span>
                    </div>
                    <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Dynamic Voter Promotion</h4>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <strong>Who Decides:</strong> The Active Raft Leader.<br/>
                      <strong>How:</strong> When a new VPC agent joins (e.g. On-Premises or Azure), it enters as a <em>Non-Voting Learner</em>. It streams WAL catchup without delaying writes. Only when log lag drops below 100 entries does the Leader execute <code>AddVoter()</code> via an atomic log commit.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #c084fc;">
                      Learner &rarr; Log Lag &lt; 100 &rarr; AddVoter() Commit
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Layer 4 -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: #f43f5e; background: rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.15); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">LAYER 4: ZERO-TRUST mTLS</span>
                      <span style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: #64748b;">Cryptographic</span>
                    </div>
                    <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">SPIFFE/SPIRE Attestation Gate</h4>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      <strong>Who Decides:</strong> SPIFFE Workload Attestation.<br/>
                      <strong>How:</strong> Every peer connection requires an X.509 SVID cert with <code>spiffe://dcouplr.internal/agent/*</code>. Unauthorized or rogue containers attempting to vote are terminated at the TLS handshake in &lt;1ms with zero WAN packets and zero log pollution.
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #f43f5e;">
                      Handshake Reject &lt; 1ms &bull; Zero Spoofing Possible
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Mathematical Foundations & Quorum Sizing Matrix -->
                <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
                  <h4 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">
                    Mathematical Foundations: Majority Formulas &amp; Sizing Matrix
                  </h4>
                  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.85rem; border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8;">
                      <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: #94a3b8; font-family: var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase;">Quorum Size Formula</div>
                      <div style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #38bdf8; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 3px;">
                        Q = &lfloor;N / 2&rfloor; + 1
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #64748b; margin-top: 3px;">Strict majority required for any commit or election</div>
                    </div>
                    <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.85rem; border-left: 3px solid #39ff14;">
                      <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: #94a3b8; font-family: var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase;">Fault Tolerance Formula</div>
                      <div style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #39ff14; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 3px;">
                        F = &lfloor;(N - 1) / 2&rfloor;
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #64748b; margin-top: 3px;">Maximum simultaneous dead or partitioned nodes</div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
                    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.84rem; color: #cbd5e1; text-align: left;">
                      <thead>
                        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);">
                          <th style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #94a3b8;">Voting Nodes (N)</th>
                          <th style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #38bdf8;">Quorum Required (Q)</th>
                          <th style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #34d399;">Tolerable Faults (F)</th>
                          <th style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #cbd5e1;">Full-Stack Suite Operational Deployment Profile</th>
                        </tr>
                      </thead>
                      <tbody>
                        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">1 Node</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #38bdf8;">1 (100%)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #f87171;">0 Failures</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #94a3b8;">Local developer testing (non-HA single laptop).</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05); background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.05);">
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #39ff14;">3 Nodes (Default)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #39ff14; font-weight: 700;">2 of 3 (66.7%)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #39ff14; font-weight: 700;">1 Node Dead (33.3%)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #f8fafc; font-weight: 600;">Standard Enterprise Production Mesh (AWS + AWS Staging + GCP Mesh). Zero single points of failure.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">5 Nodes</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #38bdf8;">3 of 5 (60.0%)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #34d399;">2 Nodes Dead (40.0%)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #94a3b8;">High-Resilience Global Banking &amp; Multi-Region Disaster Recovery Mesh.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">7 Nodes</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #38bdf8;">4 of 7 (57.1%)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #34d399;">3 Nodes Dead (42.9%)</td>
                          <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #94a3b8;">Extreme geo-distributed mesh spanning 7 global cloud regions.</td>
                        </tr>
                      </tbody>
                    </table>
                  </div>
                  <div style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.78rem; color: #f59e0b; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;">
                    <span>⚠️</span>
                    <span><strong>Why Odd Numbers?</strong> Even node counts (e.g. 4) require 3 votes for quorum yet still only tolerate 1 dead node, increasing network overhead without increasing fault tolerance. The Full-Stack Suite strictly enforces odd-sized voting sets (3, 5, 7).</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Resilience Architecture: 20ms Circuit Breakers & WAL Compaction -->
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
                  <!-- Circuit Breaker Box -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
                      <span style="color: #fbbf24; font-size: 1.1rem;">⚡</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; color: #f8fafc; margin: 0;">20ms Asymmetric Circuit Breakers</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      RPC calls between Raft peers are bounded to a strict 20ms timeout via <code>raft_transport_wrapper.go</code>. Features a per-peer Finite State Machine (<em>Closed &rarr; Open &rarr; HalfOpen</em>). When a peer fails or latency spikes, the circuit breaker trips to <strong>Open</strong>, fast-failing in &lt;1ms so slow links never stall the cluster.
                    </p>
                    <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #fbbf24; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">
                      Trip Threshold: 3 consecutive failures &bull; Cooldown: 1.5s
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- WAL Compaction Box -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.15rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
                      <span style="color: #39ff14; font-size: 1.1rem;">💾</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; color: #f8fafc; margin: 0;">Embedded BoltDB WAL Compaction</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      Every state mutation writes to an in-memory Write-Ahead Log (WAL). At <strong>10,000 delta entries</strong>, the state machine triggers an atomic snapshot, persists to embedded BoltDB, and truncates historical log indices, preventing memory ballooning and keeping RAM consumption strictly under 16MB.
                    </p>
                    <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #39ff14; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">
                      TrailingLogs: 10,240 &bull; SnapshotInterval: 120s &bull; Max RAM: &lt;16MB
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- CLI Verification & Direct Actions -->
                <div style="background: rgba(11, 17, 32, 0.9); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
                    <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #f8fafc; font-family: var(--font-mono);">
                      LIVE SRE QUORUM INSPECTION COMMAND:
                    </div>
                    <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;">
                      <a href="/docs/runbooks/EDITION_2_RAFT_CONSENSUS_QUORUM_AND_MEMBERSHIP_SPECIFICATION.html" target="_blank" style="padding: 5px 12px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; color: #000; background: #39ff14; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px;">
                        <span>📖 Open Full Web Reader ↗</span>
