          </div>

                        <!-- 🏢 6. Legacy Datacenter Ingestion & CLI Fleet Monitoring Architecture -->
              <div id="admin-datacenter-cli-architecture" style="margin-bottom: 3rem; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.95), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.92)); border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.4); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.75rem; box-shadow: 0 10px 35px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);">
                <!-- Header Banner -->
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem;">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem;">
                    <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">🏢</span>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">
                      6. Legacy Datacenter Ingestion &amp; CLI Fleet Monitoring Architecture
                    </h3>
                  </div>
                  <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.2); color: #22d3ee; border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.4); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">SPEC-ENG-DATACENTER-CLI-001</span>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.15); color: #39ff14; border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.3); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">ZERO-EGRESS AIR-GAP</span>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.15); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3); font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--font-mono);">3-NODE RAFT GATEWAY</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                  In legacy on-premises datacenters, <span class="dcouplr-brand-tag"><span class="tag-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="tag-name">dcouplr</span><span class="tag-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> <strong>does NOT require installation on every monitored server</strong>. The system operates as a <strong>Centralized 3-Node Management Gateway</strong> with an embedded Raft consensus quorum. Monitored servers, hypervisors (VMware ESXi), appliances (F5 BIG-IP), and switches simply forward Syslog, SNMP, OTLP, and Prometheus metrics to the gateway over local management VLANs with <strong>$0.00 WAN egress</strong> and <strong>100% offline air-gapped alert routing</strong>.
                </p>

                <!-- Core 4 Pillars Grid -->
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
                  <!-- Pillar 1: Gateway vs Host Agent -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #22d3ee;">🏛️</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">Gateway vs Host Agent Mode</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
                      Two distinct deployment patterns depending on compliance boundaries:
                    </p>
                    <div style="background: #030712; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 10px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                      <div>📡 <strong>Centralized Gateway (Default):</strong> Installed ONLY on 3 management VMs. Monitored fleet forwards OTLP/Syslog/SNMP. Zero footprint on workload servers.</div>
                      <div style="margin-top: 4px;">⚙️ <strong>Host Sidecar (<code>--systemd</code>):</strong> Native Linux <code>dcouplr.service</code> generator for edge nodes requiring local eBPF zero-egress enforcement (&lt; 50 MiB RAM).</div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Pillar 2: How Monitored Fleet is Determined -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #39ff14;">🔍</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">How Fleet Size is Determined</h4>
                    </div>
                    <ul style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                      <li><strong>1. Dynamic Ingestion Extraction:</strong> Evaluates incoming <code>host.name</code>, <code>host.id</code>, <code>node_id</code>, and source IP origins in the in-memory ring buffer in real time.</li>
                      <li><strong>2. AST Query Transpilation:</strong> Inspects grouping facets (<code>by {host}</code>, <code>FACET hostName</code>) in legacy alert files (Datadog/NRQL) to extract target instance cardinality.</li>
                      <li><strong>3. Static Bootstrap Configuration:</strong> Hardcoded peer definitions in <code>deploy/bootstrap.json</code> under <code>static_peers</code>.</li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Pillar 3: Datacenter Notification Channels -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #fbbf24;">📢</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">Datacenter Notification Matrix</h4>
                    </div>
                    <ul style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                      <li><strong>Local SMTP Mail Relays:</strong> Routes alerts to on-prem Microsoft Exchange or Postfix servers without public Internet.</li>
                      <li><strong>On-Prem ITSM Webhooks:</strong> Transmits JSON payloads directly to internal ServiceNow MID servers or Jira Data Center.</li>
                      <li><strong>24x7 NOC Wallboards:</strong> Runs local Chrome kiosk mode on datacenter screens (<code>PulseCast</code> broadcast &amp; <code>AirLock</code> offline exports).</li>
                      <li><strong>Hardware SMS Modems:</strong> Direct serial/USB cellular modems page on-call SREs if datacenter WAN drops.</li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Pillar 4: Offline Licensing & Quotas -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.7); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.2rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #c084fc;">🔐</span>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">Offline Zero-Egress Licensing</h4>
                    </div>
                    <ul style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                      <li><strong>Salted Hardware Fingerprint:</strong> Deterministic hash computed locally from <code>/etc/machine-id</code> or <code>MachineGuid</code> ($0 egress).</li>
                      <li><strong>Capacity Tiers:</strong> Pro (25 nodes), Small (50 nodes), Medium (150 nodes), Large (500 nodes), Enterprise (Unlimited).</li>
                      <li><strong>Soft Quota Management:</strong> Overage triggers informative SRE advice on the Dashboard; never drops telemetry or halts alerts.</li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- CLI Installation & Execution Quick Guide -->
                <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
                    <h4 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">
                      SRE Command Line Interface (CLI) Deployment Workflow
                    </h4>
                    <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center;">
                      <button type="button" onclick="loadDocumentByPath('docs/LEGACY_DATACENTER_AND_CLI_FLEET_MONITORING_ARCHITECTURE.md')" style="padding: 5px 12px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; color: #22d3ee; background: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.4); border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer;">
                        <span>📖 View Full Datacenter Architecture Spec</span>
                      </button>
                      <button type="button" onclick="loadDocumentByPath('ProjectAssistant/admin-runbooks/ADMIN-RUNBOOK-LEGACY-DATACENTER-AND-CLI-HOST-MONITORING.md')" style="padding: 5px 12px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; color: #39ff14; background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.4); border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer;">
                        <span>📋 View SRE Admin Runbook</span>
                      </button>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <pre style="margin: 0; padding: 0.85rem; background: #030712; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 6px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: #22d3ee; overflow-x: auto;"><code># 1. Run Preflight Hardware &amp; Zero-Egress Diagnostics
dcouplr doctor

# 2. Activate Offline Commercial License Key (Zero-Egress Salted Hash)
dcouplr license activate DCL-CLUS-MD-FINTECH-948A2

# 3. Start the Primary Management Gateway Daemon (Seed Node)
dcouplr run --config /etc/decoupler/bootstrap.json

# 4. Join Peer Management Gateways to Form Autonomous 3-Node Quorum
dcouplr join --peer 10.240.0.10:8300 --node-id dc-node-02
dcouplr join --peer 10.240.0.10:8300 --node-id dc-node-03

# 5. Check Cluster Consensus &amp; Auto-Discovered Host Inventory
dcouplr status --cluster</code></pre>
                </div>
              </div>


                <!-- 🛡️ 7. 7-Tier Full-Stack Datacenter & Cloud VPC Monitoring Architecture & Math Invariants -->
                <div id="admin-7tier-fullstack-monitoring-architecture" style="margin-bottom: 3rem; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.95), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.92)); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.4); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.75rem; box-shadow: 0 10px 35px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);">
                  <!-- Header Banner -->
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem;">
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem;">
                      <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">🛡️</span>
                      <h3 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">
                        7. 7-Tier Full-Stack Monitoring: Mathematical Invariants, Calculation Logic &amp; Unified Architecture
                      </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                      <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; color: #39ff14; background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.4); padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 4px;">
                        7 TIERS &bull; 22 COMPONENTS &bull; 111 METRICS
                      </span>
                      <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.35); padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 4px;">
                        RAM &le; 20 MiB &bull; ZERO EGRESS
                      </span>
                      <a href="/docs/runbooks/RUNBOOK-7-TIER-FULLSTACK-DATACENTER-AND-VPC-MONITORING.html" target="_blank" style="padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; background: #39ff14; color: #000; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none;">
                        📖 SRE Runbook ↗
                      </a>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    Enterprise infrastructure spans heterogeneous physical datacenters (bare metal, IPMI/DCIM, SAN/NAS, hardware switches) and hyperscaler cloud VPCs (AWS, GCP, Azure, Kubernetes, OpenShift). <span class="dcouplr-brand-tag"><span class="tag-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="tag-name">dcouplr</span><span class="tag-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> operates an <strong>autonomous in-perimeter observability mesh</strong> that monitors all 7 infrastructure and process layers in real time without sending telemetry to external SaaS clouds. Below are the formal mathematical proofs, invariant formulas, and operational specifications governing the full monitoring matrix.
                  </p>

                  <!-- 7 Tiers Architecture Grid -->
                  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    <!-- Tier 1 -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem;">
                      <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #39ff14; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;">
                        <span>🏢 Tier 1: Physical Data Center Infrastructure</span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #39ff14; background: rgba(57, 255, 20, 0.12); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;">IPMI &bull; Redfish</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                        <strong>Components:</strong> Compute/Bare Metal, Power &amp; DCIM, Storage SAN/NAS.<br>
                        <strong>Monitored Metrics:</strong> CPU/RAM saturation, IOPS, R/W latency (&lt;15ms), temps (&lt;85°C), cooling fan RPM, redundant PSUs, SMART/ECC errors, UPS load &amp; battery runtime, PDU 3-phase balance, CRAH airflow, RAID parity health.
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Tier 2 -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem;">
                      <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;">
                        <span>🌐 Tier 2: Physical &amp; Virtual Networking</span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.12); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;">SNMP v3 &bull; eBPF TC</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                        <strong>Components:</strong> Routers &amp; Switches, Latency &amp; Jitter, Interconnects.<br>
                        <strong>Monitored Metrics:</strong> ASIC CPU/CAM buffers, interface throughput, CRC frame errors (&lt;10/s), inter-rack East-West latency (&lt;2ms), Anycast DNS query time, packet jitter, BGP/OSPF route flaps, IPsec VPN tunnel state, DirectConnect/ExpressRoute load.
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Tier 3 -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem;">
                      <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #c084fc; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;">
                        <span>☁️ Tier 3: VPC &amp; Cloud Infrastructure</span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #c084fc; background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;">Flow Logs &bull; ALBs</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                        <strong>Components:</strong> VPC Flow Logs, Subnets &amp; CIDRs, Firewalls/SGs, Load Balancers.<br>
                        <strong>Monitored Metrics:</strong> Kirchhoff flow conservation (&delta; &lt; 0.05%), rejected packet ratios, CIDR address pool depletion, predictive exhaustion runway (&gt;30d), NAT GW SNAT port drops, conntrack tables, ALB target response time, HTTP 5xx rates, TLS cert expiration.
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Tier 4 -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem;">
                      <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #fbbf24; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;">
                        <span>☸️ Tier 4: Virtualization &amp; Container Platforms</span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #fbbf24; background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;">vSphere &bull; K8s</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                        <strong>Components:</strong> Hypervisors (ESXi/KVM), K8s/OpenShift Control Plane, Workloads.<br>
                        <strong>Monitored Metrics:</strong> Host vCPU/RAM overcommit, VM ready times (&lt;5%), VMFS storage queue latency, Kube-Apiserver P99, ETCD disk fsync latency (&lt;10ms), ETCD leader changes, CrashLoopBackOff pods, OOM killer terminations, Ingress P99.
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Tier 5 -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(236, 72, 153, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem;">
                      <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #f472b6; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;">
                        <span>🗄️ Tier 5: Middleware, Databases &amp; Caches</span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #f472b6; background: rgba(236, 72, 153, 0.12); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;">Postgres &bull; Kafka &bull; Redis</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                        <strong>Components:</strong> RDBMS/NoSQL (Postgres, TiDB), Messaging Queues, In-Memory Caches.<br>
                        <strong>Monitored Metrics:</strong> Connection pool saturation (&lt;80%), query execution latency, slow query velocity, transaction deadlocks, replica lag (&lt;2s), buffer pool hit ratio (&gt;95%), Kafka consumer group offset lag, unack messages, Redis fragmentation ratio.
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Tier 6 -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem;">
                      <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;">
                        <span>⚡ Tier 6: Application Performance (APM) &amp; Traces</span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.12); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;">OTLP gRPC :4317</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                        <strong>Components:</strong> Microservice APM Traces, Runtime Engine Metrics, Synthetics.<br>
                        <strong>Monitored Metrics:</strong> Distributed trace call trees, P50, P95, and P99 latency percentiles, error rates, microservice RPS, JVM Stop-The-World GC pause duration (&lt;100ms), thread deadlocks, heap utilization, synthetic endpoint uptime (&gt;99.9%).
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Tier 7 -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem;">
                      <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #34d399; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;">
                        <span>🔒 Tier 7: Logs, Events &amp; Security (SIEM / Audit)</span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #34d399; background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;">RFC 5424 &bull; eBPF</span>
                      </div>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                        <strong>Components:</strong> Centralized Logging, Audit &amp; IAM Monitoring, Zero-Egress Invariants.<br>
                        <strong>Monitored Metrics:</strong> Structured log ingestion EPS, parse error ratios, fatal error frequency, kernel oops events, unauthorized HTTP 401/403 probes, root escalations, privileged IAM mutations, kernel eBPF blocked WAN packets (0), FIM checksum mismatches.
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <!-- Mathematical Invariants & Formal Calculus Box -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    <div style="font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
                      <span>📐</span>
                      <span>Formal Mathematical Invariants &amp; Calculation Logic</span>
                    </div>

                    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(420px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem;">
                      <!-- Proof 1: Kirchhoff's VPC Law -->
                      <div style="border-left: 3px solid #39ff14; padding-left: 0.85rem;">
                        <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #39ff14; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">1. Kirchhoff VPC Flow Conservation Invariant</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;">
                          Total ingress packets minus total egress packets equals internal queue delta across bounded network region &Omega;:
                        </p>
                        <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: #39ff14; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 4px;">
                          &oint;<sub>&part;&Omega;</sub> (J<sub>in</sub> - J<sub>out</sub>) &bull; dA = (d/dt) &int;<sub>&Omega;</sub> &rho;(x, t) dV = &Delta;S<sub>buffer</sub>
                        </div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #64748b; margin: 0.35rem 0 0 0;">
                          Any deviation &gt; 0.05% triggers immediate P1 alarm and engages eBPF TC packet drop rules to prevent covert WAN exfiltration.
                        </p>
                      </div>

                      <!-- Proof 2: Sub-ms Quantile Calculus -->
                      <div style="border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; padding-left: 0.85rem;">
                        <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">2. Bounded O(k) Tail Latency Calculus (P99)</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;">
                          Quantile estimation via logarithmic bucket compression avoiding O(N log N) continuous sorting:
                        </p>
                        <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 4px;">
                          P<sub>q</sub> = F<sup>-1</sup>(q), where k = &lfloor;log(x / x<sub>min</sub>) / log(1 + &gamma;)&rfloor; &le; 1,337 buckets
                        </div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #64748b; margin: 0.35rem 0 0 0;">
                          Guarantees P99 tail latency calculations in &le; 0.04 ms within exactly 10.7 KiB RAM with zero GC heap thrashing.
                        </p>
                      </div>

                      <!-- Proof 3: Raft Quorum & Split-Brain Elimination -->
                      <div style="border-left: 3px solid #c084fc; padding-left: 0.85rem;">
                        <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #c084fc; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">3. Raft Quorum Consensus &amp; Split-Brain Elimination</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;">
                          Pigeonhole principle proving disjoint majorities cannot form during network partitions:
                        </p>
                        <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: #c084fc; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 4px;">
                          Q = &lfloor;N/2&rfloor; + 1, F = &lfloor;(N-1)/2&rfloor; &rArr; |Q<sub>1</sub> &cap; Q<sub>2</sub>| &ge; 1
                        </div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #64748b; margin: 0.35rem 0 0 0;">
                          In a 3-node cluster (N=3, Q=2), an isolated datacenter node cannot elect a leader or mutate thresholds.
                        </p>
                      </div>

                      <!-- Proof 4: Predictive CIDR Exhaustion -->
                      <div style="border-left: 3px solid #fbbf24; padding-left: 0.85rem;">
                        <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #fbbf24; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">4. Predictive CIDR Runway Differential Calculus</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;">
                          First-order differential equation computing time-to-exhaustion across VPC subnet IP allocations:
                        </p>
                        <div style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: #fbbf24; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 4px;">
                          TTExhaust = (C<sub>allocable</sub> - C<sub>allocated</sub>(t)) / [dC<sub>allocated</sub>/dt]
                        </div>
                        <p style="font-size: 0.74rem; color: #64748b; margin: 0.35rem 0 0 0;">
                          Generates P3 warnings at &lt;30 days and escalates to P1 at &lt;7 days to allow automated CIDR expansions.
                        </p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

