                  <!-- Fleet Isolation & False Alarm Elimination -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.06); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8; font-size: 0.92rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      🛡️ Customer Fleet Isolation &amp; Zero False-Alarm Enforcement
                    </div>
                    <div style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.6;">
                      When an enterprise configures their active database technologies via <code>POST /v1/telemetry/database/technologies/select</code>, unselected engines are automatically suppressed:
                      <ul style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem;">
                        <li><strong>Tier 5 Matrix Suppression:</strong> Matrix components (<code>databases_oracle</code>, <code>databases_mssql</code>, etc.) are toggled to <code>enabled: false</code>, preventing artificial degradation of composite health.</li>
                        <li><strong>71-Node Census Status:</strong> Unselected technologies across all nodes are tagged with <code>INACTIVE (EXCLUDED FROM CUSTOMER FLEET)</code>, preventing false positive incident tickets.</li>
                        <li><strong>Pre-Built Presets:</strong> Supports <code>postgres_only</code>, <code>postgres_redis</code>, <code>oracle_enterprise</code>, <code>mssql_stack</code>, <code>lamp_stack</code>, <code>all_engines</code>, and <code>clear_all</code>.</li>
                      </ul>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>


                <!-- 📺 Section 8.7: 24x7 NOC Wallboard Ergonomics, Display Architectures & Kiosk Carousel Runbook -->
                <div id="admin-wallboard-ergonomics-dossier" style="margin-bottom: 3rem; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.96), rgba(11, 17, 32, 0.94)); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.45); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.75rem; box-shadow: 0 10px 35px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3); padding-bottom: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem;">
                    <div>
                      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">
                        <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; color: #c084fc; background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px; text-transform: uppercase;">
                          SECTION 8.7 &bull; ARCHITECTURAL DOSSIER
                        </span>
                        <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #39ff14; font-weight: 700;">
                          SPEC: VA-SPEC-WALLBOARD-OBS-001
                        </span>
                      </div>
                      <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: #ffffff; margin: 0;">
                        24x7 NOC Wallboard Ergonomics: Option A (The Sweet Spot) &amp; Option B (Kiosk Carousel)
                      </h2>
                    </div>
                    <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem;">
                      <a href="/wallboard?layout=sweet-spot" target="_blank" style="padding: 6px 14px; font-size: 0.78rem; text-decoration: none; background: #38bdf8; color: #000; font-weight: 700; border-radius: 4px;">
                        ⚡ Launch Option A
                      </a>
                      <a href="/wallboard?layout=carousel&interval=30s" target="_blank" style="padding: 6px 14px; font-size: 0.78rem; text-decoration: none; background: #7c3aed; color: #fff; font-weight: 700; border-radius: 4px;">
                        🔄 Launch Option B
                      </a>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    In large-scale mission control and SRE operations, wallboard screens must resolve <strong>Macro Glanceability vs. Micro Depth</strong>. Displaying all 122 granular metric gauges simultaneously creates cognitive overload ("wall of tiny numbers"), while displaying only top-level health blinds operators to emerging subsystem deadlocks. <span class="dcouplr-brand-tag"><span class="tag-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="tag-name">dcouplr</span><span class="tag-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> provides two standardized display architectures:
                  </p>

                  <!-- Side-by-Side Comparison Grid -->
                  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(360px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    <!-- Option A: The Sweet Spot -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                        <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.15); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">
                          🏆 OPTION A: THE SWEET SPOT
                        </span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: #34d399; font-family: var(--font-mono);">NOC Desks &bull; War Rooms</span>
                      </div>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;">
                        Macro Canvas + 7-Tier Micro-LED Ribbon + Dynamic Incident Spotlight
                      </h4>
                      <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                        Combines <strong>Recommendation 1 (Management-by-Exception)</strong> with <strong>Recommendation 2 (7-Tier Micro-LED Ribbon)</strong> on an ergonomic single-screen canvas:
                      </p>
                      <ul style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                        <li><strong>Header Micro-LED Matrix:</strong> 24 pulsing micro-LED indicators mapped across Tiers 01&ndash;07 providing instant full-stack health in minimal vertical pixels.</li>
                        <li><strong>3-Column Macro Canvas:</strong> Multi-VPC mesh topology, live 60 FPS throughput waveform, and Raft consensus quorum status.</li>
                        <li><strong>Dynamic Incident Spotlight:</strong> Displays <code>🟢 122/122 Invariants Nominal</code> when healthy; instantly explodes into high-contrast exception triage on any metric breach.</li>
                      </ul>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #64748b;">
                        Deployment: <code style="color: #38bdf8;">/wallboard?layout=sweet-spot</code>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Option B: Multi-Scene Kiosk Carousel -->
                    <div style="background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                        <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #c084fc; background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.15); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px;">
                          🔄 OPTION B: KIOSK CAROUSEL
                        </span>
                        <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: #c084fc; font-family: var(--font-mono);">Unattended Video Walls</span>
                      </div>
                      <h4 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;">
                        Multi-Scene Kiosk Carousel (Auto-Rotating every 30s)
                      </h4>
                      <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                        An automated rotating multi-scene carousel engine that cycles every 30 seconds across three dedicated operational scenes:
                      </p>
                      <ul style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                        <li><strong>Scene 1 (Macro Canvas):</strong> Multi-VPC network topology, BGP peering, and cross-cloud transit latency.</li>
                        <li><strong>Scene 2 (7-Tier Deep Dive):</strong> Granular 24-component card grid with live metrics, cache hit ratios, and worker connection saturation.</li>
                        <li><strong>Scene 3 (VOE Incident Queue):</strong> Live incident backlog, automated diagnosis logs, priority-ranked remediation tickets, and 71-node census status.</li>
                        <li><strong>Emergency Critical Freeze:</strong> Rotation automatically freezes if any P1 Critical breach occurs until cleared.</li>
                      </ul>
                      <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #64748b;">
