                  <!-- Transport Architecture Summary (AirLock vs PulseCast) -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div style="font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; font-size: 0.92rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                      📡 Zero-Cost Transport Patterns for 24x7 Wallboards
                    </div>
                    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.82rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.5;">
                      <div>
                        <strong style="color: #38bdf8;">Pattern A: <span class="dcouplr-wordmark"><span class="dcouplr-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="dcouplr-text">dcouplr</span><span class="dcouplr-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> AirLock&trade; (NOC Desk)</strong><br>
                        Outbound TLS 1.3 WireGuard tunnel via Cloudflare Zero Trust. Non-expiring Service Token authentication eliminates 3:00 AM corporate SSO session timeouts. 100% inbound ports closed.
                      </div>
                      <div>
                        <strong style="color: #c084fc;">Pattern B: <span class="dcouplr-wordmark"><span class="dcouplr-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="dcouplr-text">dcouplr</span><span class="dcouplr-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> PulseCast&trade; (Edge CDN)</strong><br>
                        Air-gapped unidirectional snapshot. In-VPC control node pushes a sanitized 1.14 KB JSON pulse every 5s to Cloudflare R2 ($0 egress) or AWS S3. Wallboard TVs fetch purely from CDN edge.
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
