                  <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                    Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) and Customer Relationship Management (CRM) engines represent the financial and transactional backbone of global enterprises.
                    To eliminate the historical chaos of misallocated metrics and phantom alerts, <span class="dcouplr-wordmark"><span class="dcouplr-bracket">&lt;</span><span class="dcouplr-text">dcouplr</span><span class="dcouplr-bracket">/&gt;</span></span> enforces two non-negotiable architectural invariants:
                    (1) <strong>Strict 7-Tier Demarcation</strong> separating the in-memory database storage tier from the application server and business workflow tier, and
                    (2) <strong>Opt-In Fleet Isolation</strong> (silenced by default) so non-ERP organizations experience zero operational alert noise.
                  </p>

                  <!-- 7-Tier Demarcation Banner -->
                  <div style="background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.25); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    <div style="font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 800; color: #38bdf8; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; font-family: var(--font-mono); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                      📐 Architectural Placement: Tier 5 (Database) vs. Tier 6 (Application Server &amp; APM)
                    </div>
                    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
                      <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8); border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;">
                        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #38bdf8; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
                          🗄️ Tier 5: Middleware &amp; Databases (Storage &amp; Persistence Plane)
                        </div>
                        <ul style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                          <li><strong>SAP HANA:</strong> Column store memory allocation %, disk savepoint flush time, delta merge backlog, row/column store CPU locks.</li>
                          <li><strong>Oracle Database / RAC:</strong> Buffer cache hit %, library cache locks, redo log switch contention, undo retention.</li>
                          <li><strong>Microsoft SQL Server:</strong> Buffer cache hit ratio, page life expectancy, latch contention, TempDB allocation.</li>
                          <li><strong>Relational &amp; NoSQL Core:</strong> PostgreSQL, Redis, MySQL, Cassandra, PingCAP TiDB.</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>
                      <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8); border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;">
                        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #c084fc; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
                          ⚡ Tier 6: App Services &amp; APM (Application Server &amp; Process Plane)
                        </div>
                        <ul style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #94a3b8; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem;">
                          <li><strong>SAP S/4HANA &amp; ECC:</strong> ABAP dispatcher work processes (DIA/UPD/BTC/ENQ), Central Services ASCS/ERS lock table, RFC Gateway (SM58), IDoc Status 51 errors, Fiori OData p95 response time.</li>
                          <li><strong>Oracle EBS R12 / Fusion:</strong> Concurrent Manager queue lag, Inactive No Manager status, Forms runtime locks, Workflow Mailer.</li>
                          <li><strong>Microsoft Dynamics 365 F&amp;O:</strong> AOS worker thread utilization, DMF staging error backlog, batch execution delay.</li>
                          <li><strong>Enterprise CRM &amp; HCM:</strong> Salesforce Platform Event Bus, Workday EIB/RaaS, ServiceNow CSM Table API.</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>
                    </div>
